### G02E13 · Radio Crow Elder Vocal Type ''Startup Sound''

- Source batch: M003
- Former role class: aging-stage type
- Links: {"houses":["HC02"],"scenarios":["G02-SC2","G02-SC1","G02-SC3"],"states":["S02","S07"],"synthetics":["H02"],"theaters":["XT02"]}

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Common species |
| Battlefield unit | Pack or unit |
| Battlefield role | Alarm Delay |
| Common species, variants and command scope | The elder vocal type ''Startup Sound'' stiffens its throat only at the sound of a transformer starting and keeps its wings folded even at a real fire alarm. It cannot lead the flock, and its silence worsens misclassification. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0290"></a>

### Role and Body

The aged individual beside the old transformer, whose neck stiffened only at the start-up hum, stayed on the insulator with its wings folded even when a real fire bell rang. The price of reacting late to unfamiliar alarms the more one specialized in familiar call patterns gathered in this body, and the flock scattered only after short-circuit smoke had covered the roof.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0292"></a>

### Origin

It was a remnant of the days when the pattern of three horn blasts, two inspection bells, and the transformer start-up hum was learned as food and danger. The imitation in the communal roost carried the new call patterns over into the young individuals, but it could not carry them into this aged syrinx, and that lag became the fictional role of damage.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0294"></a>

### Habitat

By day it clung to the insulators inside the transformer fence, and even when the night insect lamps came on it sat by the start-up hum rather than the lamps. It hardly ever appeared on the bridge or the school passage, and came down to the factory-roof exhaust vents only in the outage weeks when the start-up hum stopped.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0296"></a>

### Needs and Economy

For this body not to slow the flock''s scattering, a three-day training in a new low tone and the alley custom of using crow calls as an intrusion alarm had to be adjusted at the same time. Training alone reduced control malfunctions but left the cheap watch of the alleys, and removing the custom alone reduced malfunctions but took away the ears that had warned of intruders first.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0298"></a>

### Life Cycle and Maintenance

The elasticity of the syrinx dropped by one note each season, and the lowered note grew further from the new alarm bells. Its feathers were kept up with sand baths, but its auditory learning did not recover, and when it dried an injured wing on the transformer''s heat, that heat became one more false safety signal.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0300"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

The aged individual could not lead the flock, and its silence instead fed the misjudgment. Even when the young individuals took to the air at the alarm bell, as long as this body stayed seated, the H02 classification kept the outage warning, and human control easily took that as grounds for halting work.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0302"></a>

### Escalating Threat

If its wings stayed folded even once the alarm bell rang, the misclassification began. Without the three-day training, the scattering came only after the smoke became visible, and that delay made a gap in both the transmission halt and the detection of intrusions in the alleys at once.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0304"></a>

### Combat and Response

The aged individual attuned only to the transformer start-up hum stayed on the insulator with its wings folded even when a real fire bell rang. Sending a short low tone different from the start-up hum from outside the fence every dawn for three days made its wing-folding a beat later. If the new low tone could not be played for three days, the short-circuit smoke covered the roof first, and only then did the flock scatter.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0306"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

Whether to remove from the control network the custom of the alley residents using crow calls as an intrusion alarm was borne by the night duty officer without a signature. Not removing it let the misclassification of G02-SC2 halt the factories and the railway together, and reversing it within 48 hours allowed one more malfunction. Removing it reduced the malfunctions, and the cheap watch that G02-SC2 had kept disappeared from the alleys.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0308"></a>

### Scenario Links

G02-SC2 completed the false outage at the point where the machine classification that raised calls to outage warnings overlapped with the aged individual''s silence. The horn pattern of G02-SC1 was the call pattern this syrinx forgot last, and the new inspection bell of G02-SC3 did not reach this body without the three-day training.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G02-heading-0310"></a>
