<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0019"></a>
<a id="g08e15"></a>

### G08E15 · Raider Scouts

- Source batch: M013
- Former role class: Strategic encounter
- Links: {"houses":["HC08"],"scenarios":["G08-SC2","G08-SC3","G08-SC1"],"states":["S08","S13"],"synthetics":["H08"],"theaters":["XT03"]}

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Person |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Movement time at the end of the alley and the duct mouth |
| Common species, variants and command scope | The end of the lower windbreak alley and the ventilation-duct mouth on the Jegi-dong side |

- The raider scouts stand at the end of the alley.
- The raider scouts look toward the ventilation-duct mouth.
- On the duct foothold the sacks lie in one line before the raider scouts.
- The curtain-layer count is written on the board in front of the raider scouts.
- The raider scouts'' footsteps carry as far as the door row.
- The board with the changed differential-pressure figures is in the raider scouts'' hands.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0023"></a>

## Habitat record

The record board of the Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer lies on the shelf beside the latch in the Dongdaemun night-wage corridor. The remaining positive-pressure doors, the differential-pressure figures, and an armed group are written together on the record board. The raider chief, at the front of the group, stands toward the door gap, and the raider scouts look from the end of the lower windbreak alley toward the ventilation-duct mouth.

The Dongdaemun Raiders are gathered in the lower windbreak alley and along the row of remaining positive-pressure doors. In the season when the filter count falls, the footholds run on into the ventilation duct of the sealed side chamber on the Jegi-dong side. On a night when dust from the relay docks of the Korea Strait Theater is piled at the entrance, the entrance curtains are layered and the group stands before those curtains. The movement time is written in figures on the differential-pressure board, and the alley runs on into the White Cross corridor.

The raider chief is before the differential-pressure board and the sack cords. The raider elite squad, on both sides of the chief, handles the curtains and the filter crates. The raider scouts are on the foothold at the end of the alley and are writing the curtain-layer count on a board.

Inside the sacks are filter crates with the Changdong Protection House mark and work lamps of the White Cross night-wage corridor. The filter count is written as the same figure on the White Cross night-wage duty officer''s record board and on the raider chief''s board. The work lamps lie across the mouths of the sacks.

At the start of the night the raider scouts stand at the end of the alley. After the sacks line up before the doors, the raider elite squad stands at each door. After the entrance curtains are layered, the raider chief stands before the differential-pressure board.

The hand of the White Cross night-wage duty officer is on the latch of the positive-pressure door, and the work lamp lights the inner alley. The Changdong Protection House supply duty officer is before the inner shelf of the sealed side chamber. The filter crates are set on that shelf.

The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer is writing the differential-pressure figures on both the raider chief''s board and the duty record board. The White Cross night-wage duty officer and the Changdong Protection House supply duty officer stand on the inner side of the door where the board hangs. The raider chief stands on the outer side of the board.

By the count of filters that went into the sacks, the filters on the positive-pressure doors remain as a single layer. The White Cross night-wage duty officer writes the differential-pressure board again together with the curtain layers. The entrance curtains are layered one more time, and the Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer stands inside the door with the record board left on the shelf beside the latch.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0032"></a>

## Linked scenarios

<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0033"></a>

### G08-SC1 · Filters on the shelf

- Stage: 1
- Trigger: On an early-winter night the filter crates of the Changdong Protection House are before the positive-pressure doors of the Dongdaemun night-wage corridor, and the Dongdaemun Raiders stand before the crates. The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer and Choidaon are beside the differential-pressure board of the same door.
- Actors: S08, HC08, H08
- Ecological mechanism: The raider chief reads the differential-pressure figures, and the raider elite squad takes the crate cords. While the filters are on the shelf, the positive-pressure doors stay shut toward the outside.
- Choices: The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer moves the filter crates to the inner shelf of the sealed side chamber on the Jegi-dong side. / The Changdong Protection House supply duty officer writes the crate count half on the shelf and half on the raider sacks. / Choidaon advances the movement time on the differential-pressure board and shuts the positive-pressure doors.
- Outcomes: After the crates are moved to the shelf, the raiders stand before the doors, the filter crates are on the side-chamber shelf, and the positive pressure holds. After the count is written by halves, the crates are divided between the shelf and the sacks, and the raider elite squad stands in the alley. After the doors are shut, the raiders stand at the ventilation-duct mouth and Choidaon is beside the shut door.
- Moral cost: In the count divided by halves, the protection filters of the Changdong Protection House remain as a single layer, and after the doors are shut the passage on the Jegi-dong side lies on the side of the raiders'' sacks.
- Source dossier: G08

<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0035"></a>

### G08-SC2 · Curtains of the night wage

- Stage: 2
- Trigger: On a night when the White Cross night-wage duty officer is before the entrance curtains, the raider scouts stand at the end of the lower windbreak alley. The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer and the Changdong Protection House supply duty officer are beside the differential-pressure board of the same entrance.
- Actors: S08, S13, HC08
- Ecological mechanism: The raider scouts count the curtain layers and write them on a board, and the raider chief sets the place of the night-wage sacks before the doors. The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer leaves the differential-pressure figures on the record board.
- Choices: The White Cross night-wage duty officer keeps the curtains at three layers and opens the night-wage passage toward the Changdong Protection House supply duty officer. / The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer writes the differential-pressure figures on both the raider chief''s board and the duty record board. / The Changdong Protection House supply duty officer moves the night-wage sacks onto the shelf of the sealed side chamber.
- Outcomes: After the passage is opened toward the Changdong Protection House, the raider elite squad stands outside the curtains and the night-wage goods are on the side-chamber side. After the figures are written on both boards, the raider chief and the White Cross night-wage duty officer stand before the same board, and the sacks remain at the doors. After the sacks are moved into the side chamber, the Changdong Protection House supply duty officer stands before the curtains and the raider scouts are at the duct mouth.
- Moral cost: Where the passage is opened, the night-wage goods remain in the sack count, and where the figures are written together the duty officer spends the night beside the door.
- Source dossier: G08

<a id="Hostile-Group-G08-heading-0037"></a>

### G08-SC3 · Dust at the entrance

- Stage: 3
- Trigger: On a night when dust from the relay docks of the Korea Strait Theater is piled at the entrance of the Dongdaemun night-wage corridor, a higher figure is written on the entrance differential-pressure board. The White Cross, the Central Intelligence Bureau, the Changdong Protection House, and Choidaon are at the same entrance.
- Actors: S08, S13, XT03, HC08, H08
- Ecological mechanism: The raiders layer the curtains over the dust and set the sacks at the entrance between the layers. While the curtains are layered and the filter crates are at the entrance, the positive-pressure doors stay shut toward the outside.
- Choices: The White Cross night-wage duty officer layers the curtains from the inner side of the raiders'' hands and keeps the entrance on the duty side. / The Central Intelligence Bureau patrol duty officer moves the Korea Strait Theater relay crates that have no dust on them to the Changdong Protection House shelf. / Choidaon writes the figures on the differential-pressure board toward the shut door and leaves the raiders'' sacks at the ventilation-duct mouth.
- Outcomes: After the curtains are layered from the inside, the entrance is on the side of the White Cross night-wage duty officer and the raider elite squad stands at the outer layer. After the crates are moved to the shelf, the dust-marked sacks are at the entrance and the protection crates are on the Changdong Protection House shelf. After the figures on the differential-pressure board are written toward the shut door, the raiders are gathered at the duct mouth on the Jegi-dong side and Choidaon is beside the entrance board.
- Moral cost: The sacks of the raider elite squad standing at the outer layer hold the night-wage work lamps, and after the group gathers toward the duct the passage of the sealed side chamber runs on into the raiders'' foothold.
- Source dossier: G08
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G09', 'G09 · Sangam Deserters', 'bestiary', 9, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G09-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G09-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

The Sangam Deserters stand in the cold corridor of the Sangam cooling annex, wearing military clothing and carrying equipment and weapons. In midwinter they stand between the shelves of the corridor, and around the thaw they stand at the Achasan inspection window and the cold warehouse. In the room-temperature passage outside the inspection window the deserter scouts assigned to the doorway stand, and the deserter squad leader and the deserter elite squad stand inside the warehouse and the corridor.

The deserter squad leader stands in the center of the cold corridor, the deserter elite squad stands beside the goods to the squad leader''s left and right, and the deserter scouts stand on the door side and the track side. When the deserter elite squad sets the goods at the Achasan inspection window, the deserter squad leader stands beside the remaining fuel drums and the deserter scouts stand at the end of that passage. The deserters in the three places wear the same military clothing and keep equipment with the same inventory marks.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G09-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | The inventory watch of the Seoul Station Inventory House sees this group on a midwinter night in the cold corridor of the Sangam cooling annex. People with cold-weather outer layers over their uniforms stand before the inventory shelves, and at their feet are fuel drums and ammunition boxes marked by the Seoul Station Inventory House. The person standing in the center has set a radio set beside the feet and is looking toward the removal passage. |
| Habitat and movement | The group gathers in the cold corridor of the Sangam cooling annex. When the thaw comes and the heat needle on the inspection-window panel rises, the group stands divided between the Achasan inspection window and the cold warehouse. After the mineral and fuel trains of the Duman River Far East Theater pass the outer track carrying the cold, the deserter scouts stand at the outer door of the corridor and the deserter elite squad is inside the cold warehouse. |
| Food and energy | The fuel drums, cooling tools, and cold-weather clothing marked by the Seoul Station Inventory House, which were on the shelves of the cold corridor, lie at the feet of the Sangam Deserters. Those quantities are written in the removal column of the inventory ledger, and the same quantities are written as the cold quantity in the equity column of the Yeouido Investment Federation. On a day when a train of the Duman River Far East Theater stands, a row of mineral boxes is on the floor of the Achasan inspection window, and the number of fuel drums matches the number written in the removal column of the ledger. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | In midwinter uniforms and cold-weather outer layers lie between the shelves of the cold corridor, and the equipment piles lie as far as the front of the valve. When the thaw comes and the heat needle on the inspection-window panel rises, the group stands divided between the Achasan inspection window and the cold warehouse. After the train passes carrying the cold, the deserter elite squad remains at the inspection window and the deserter scouts gather at the door of the cold warehouse. |
| Senses | The Sangam Deserters watch the removal passage and the cooling-valve side of the cold corridor in the Sangam cooling annex. The group stands beside the shelves that carry the Seoul Station Inventory House mark, with the fuel drums and tool shelves in the middle, and stands with its back toward the Achasan inspection window. When a train of the Duman River Far East Theater stands on the track outside the corridor, the deserter scouts watch the track-side door. |
| Group behavior | The deserter squad leader stands in the center of the cold corridor, and ammunition boxes and a radio set are at the squad leader''s feet. The deserter elite squad stands at the shelves to the squad leader''s left and right, beside the fuel drums and tool piles. The deserter scouts stand divided between the removal passage and the track-side door, facing the squad leader''s side while watching the outside. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G09-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

The deserter squad leader stands inside the cold corridor beside the fuel drums, ammunition boxes, radio set, and shelf tools. The deserter elite squad stands at the Achasan inspection window and the cold warehouse where those goods are set, and the deserter scouts stand at the removal passage and the track-side door. In front of the deserter squad leader lies the inventory-ledger page on which the warehouse time columns of the Yeouido Investment Federation and the Achasan Gate are written.

| Individual | Type | Battlefield unit | Battlefield role | Former role class | Source batch |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| [G09E01 · Deserter Squad Leader](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G09/#g09e01) | Person | Pack or unit | Stands beside the inventory-ledger page and the ammunition boxes, in the center of the cold corridor and in front of the equipment pile. | Leader | M013 |
| [G09E08 · Deserter Elite Squad](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G09/#g09e08) | Person | Pack or unit | Stands at the shelves and at the Achasan inspection window, with the fuel drums, cooling tools, and piles of cold-weather clothing beside them. | Elite | M014 |
| [G09E15 · Deserter Scouts](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G09/#g09e15) | Person | Single individual | Stands divided between the removal passage and the track-side door and watches the outer door and the train. | Strategic encounter | M015 |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G09-heading-0011"></a>
<a id="g09e01"></a>

### G09E01 · Deserter Squad Leader

- Source batch: M013
- Former role class: Leader
