### G15E05 · Patch-Frequency Nursing Car

- Source batch: M023
- Former role class: occupational special type
- Links: {"houses":["HP01"],"scenarios":["G15-SC1","G15-SC2"],"states":["S15","S04"],"synthetics":["H15"],"theaters":["XT05"]}

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Patch Relay |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A nursing cart with multiple biosignal-patch receiving antennas and a drawer of replacement patches. It uploads the urgent list to the rounds warden and treats anyone without a patch as a person outside the protection roster, and after three overlapping false positives it drops its frequency and applies no new patches until a human confirms. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0098"></a>

### Role and Body

A trade specialist: a nursing cart with multiple biosignal-patch receiving antennas and a drawer of replacement patches.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0100"></a>

### Origin

Equipment that relayed patch signals in the crowded sickbeds was left behind, unable to tell tool noise from biosignals.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0102"></a>

### Habitat and Needs

It shuttles between the welfare wing and the Ttukseom workshop, needing sensor patches, antenna calibrators, and batteries.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0104"></a>

### Life and Maintenance

After three overlapping false positives it drops its frequency and applies no new patches until a human confirms.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0106"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

It uploads the urgent list to the rounds warden and treats anyone without a patch as a person outside the protection roster.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0108"></a>

### Escalation

Stage 1 remeasures, stage 2 force-applies patches, and stage 3 quarantines the no-signal zones.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0110"></a>

### Engagement and Response

Stopping the tool noise and sending a calibration signal wins compliance, and radio jamming erases real urgent signals too.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0112"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

Health alerts can be kept on, but the right to refuse wearing a patch and the log-retention period must be set.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0114"></a>

### Scenario Links

G15-SC1, G15-SC2.

