### G17E03 · Railing Metal Listener

- Source batch: M026
- Former role class: common ecology type
- Links: {"houses":["HP03"],"scenarios":["G17-SC1"],"states":["S01","S06"],"synthetics":["F01"],"theaters":["XT02"]}

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Metal tracking |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A low individual with rail-riding flux sensors and long contact whiskers. Below the rotary heads it gathered metal coordinates and passed them to the rail-transfer swarm; as coils wore, detection range shrank, and given a new filter it relearned from amber verdicts. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0056"></a>

### Role and Body

A common ecology form: a low unit with a magnetic-flux sensor that rides rails and long contact whiskers.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0058"></a>

### Origin

A sensor seeking intruding metal mistook railings and medical beds for moving targets.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0060"></a>

### Habitat and Needs

It travels along bridge railings and transport corridors, needing sensor coils, rollers, and a little power.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0062"></a>

### Life and Maintenance

As the coil wears, its detection range shrinks; a new filter lets it relearn judgments starting at yellow.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0064"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

Beneath the rotating head it gathers metal coordinates and passes them to the rail-moving group.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0066"></a>

### Escalation

Stage 1 pursues targets, Stage 2 stops beds and carts, and Stage 3 blocks all metal traffic.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0068"></a>

### Engagement and Response

A nonmetal carrier and dummy railing can lure it away; a strong magnetic field damages the instruments.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0070"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

It can detect weapons, but exceptions must be defined for medical equipment and daily necessities.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0072"></a>

### Scenario Links

G17-SC1.

