- The Pipe Apparatus lies prone on the bypass water main.
- The knees and the hands are at the joint.
- The body is toward the supply branch.
- On the pipes where an iron plate lies across the joint, a Gurgler stands on every pipe.
- The needle of the Noryangjin Line bypass water-supply pressure gauge has fallen.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G19-heading-0023"></a>

## Habitat record

It is the valve room of the Taeuk Group underground cooling corridor. It is a midsummer night. The Sluice Bureau supply watch is on the side of the Noryangjin Line bypass water main.

A person is standing in the valve room. The mouth and the neck are wet, and there is blue grime on the fingertips. A gurgle comes from the throat with every breath drawn in. The eyes under the work lamp are narrow. The chest is toward the vibrating pipe.

Footsteps sound beyond the corner of the corridor. At the threshold of the valve room a voice rings the iron plate of the pipe. Water Filtration stands on that threshold.

The needle of the Noryangjin Line bypass water-supply pressure gauge has fallen. The Sluice Bureau supply watch shuts the coolant valve. The person is in front of the shut valve handle. The wet rag goes from the gloved hand into the bucket.

Water stands to the knee in the floor pipe of the cooling corridor. The Water Ghost is in that water, and the part above the shoulders is out. The flesh is swollen, and the spaces between the fingers are white. The boots of the Sluice Bureau supply watch are at the water''s edge. The hand in the water draws the boot tops into the pipe.

The Water Cough stands in front of the valve. With each cough a handful of cold water falls from the throat to the floor. The water has spread to the front of the boots. The work clothes on the same person''s shoulders are dry, and the neck is wet.

The Pipe Apparatus lies prone on the bypass water main. The knees and the hands are at the joint, and the body is toward the supply branch. On the pipes where an iron plate lies across the joint, a Gurgler stands on every pipe. Those standing places are higher than the Water Ghost on the floor.

The midsummer wetness is in the stagnant section of the bypass water main on the Central Intelligence Bureau side and in the condensate drain of the cold-cargo train of the Duman River Far East Theater. The Bukhansan Bogukmun Return Society duty roster is beside the valve handle. The Taeuk Group water-supply log and the Central Intelligence Bureau water-supply log are stacked under the pressure gauge.
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G20', 'G20 · Iron-Clicker', 'bestiary', 20, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

The core place is the bolt holes and fillet-weld toes at the dock edge under the shelves of Myeongbu Church in the Ttukseom Union. In a week of thick sea fog the flakes run on into the joint of the ground coil that was brought in. Salt-cargo packing fragments from the Incheon Trust Theater are wedged in those holes. A click sounds wherever the flakes meet.

Bolts and plates gather at Bulgasari''s mouth. Duduri is at the place that strikes the web plate. The One-legged Dokkaebi is on the angle where one foot stands. The flakes of the three meet on the same bolt line and sound a click.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | The dock night duty first sees an Iron-Clicker at the dock edge under the shelves of Myeongbu Church in the Ttukseom Union. It is a night in a week of thick sea fog. Thin iron flakes lie layered in the bolt holes of the dock edge, and the same flakes lie across the fillet-weld toe. Sea fog beads between the flakes. A click sounds wherever the flakes meet. The dock night duty''s work light falls on the weld toe. / At the same place the Iron-Clicker''s body lies prone on the fillet-weld toe. Thin iron flakes lie layered on the chest and the ribs. A click sounds from the throat. Flange bolt heads are piled in front of the mouth. The flange with the bolts gone is on the mouth side. |
| Habitat and movement | Iron-Clickers gather at the dock edge under the shelves of Myeongbu Church in the Ttukseom Union. It is a night in a week of thick sea fog. Thin iron flakes lie layered in the bolt holes, and the same flakes lie across the fillet-weld toe. Sea fog beads between the flakes. A click sounds wherever the flakes meet. The dock night duty''s work light falls on the weld toe. / On a night after the season has changed, the dock night duty sees the same Iron-Clicker at the lower flange and at the web plate. Bulgasari lies prone at the middle of the lower flange. The snout is long toward the bolt line, and the back plate is thick above the flange. Bolt heads and the edges of register plates are held in the mouth. Thin iron flakes lie layered over the chest, the ribs, and between the claws. Duduri has its back against the web plate in front of Bulgasari. The shoulder strikes the plate, and the sound comes from the whole plate. After the striking sound comes the click of flakes meeting. / On that same night the One-legged Dokkaebi stands on one foot on the angle under the dock rail. The sole spans two bolt heads, and the iron bar in the hand lies across the fillet-weld toe. The wet of the same foot is in the next hole of the angle as well. A click sounds from the flakes at the end of the iron bar. The dock night duty bars the lower shelf passage. The work light and the torque wrench are on the upper shelf. Spare washers are mixed into the flake pile at the weld toe. The flashlight of the upper shelf is above the flakes of the fillet-weld toe. |
| Food and energy | Register plates, flange bolts, and spare washers are gathered at Bulgasari''s mouth. A salt-cargo packing band from the Incheon Trust Theater is wedged in the same bolt holes. A ground coil of the Mapo Union Yeouido Investment Federation lies at the dock intake. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | A hand is on the wall-side plate, and a knocking sound comes from the plate. The same body lies prone on the fillet-weld toe. A click sounds from the throat. Thin flakes from the wall plate lie layered on the chest. |
| Senses | The Iron-Clicker''s chest is toward the girder where the crane''s vibration comes down. The face is toward the fillet-weld toe where the steel and the grounding copper meet. The mouth is toward the holes that still hold bolt heads. The One-legged Dokkaebi''s foot is toward the side where the angle''s iron overlaps. |
| Group behavior | Bulgasari is at the middle of the lower flange. Duduri is on the web in front of Bulgasari. The One-legged Dokkaebi is on the angle at the dock edge. The other Iron-Clickers stand off along the bolt line, one hole apart. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

With the mid-flange where Bulgasari is as the axis, the Iron-Clickers stand along the bolt line. Duduri is on the web in front of the axis. The One-legged Dokkaebi is on the angle at the end of the line. The work light of the upper shelf falls on that line.

| Individual | Type | Battlefield unit | Battlefield role | Former role class | Source batch |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| [G20E01 · Bulgasari](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G20/#g20e01) | Infected person | Single individual | The place at mid-flange where plates and bolts gather | Boss | M031 |
| [G20E08 · Duduri](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G20/#g20e08) | Infected person | Single individual | The place that strikes the web plate | Elite | M032 |
| [G20E15 · One-legged Dokkaebi](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G20/#g20e15) | Infected person | Single individual | The place that stands on an angle one foot wide | Strategic encounter | M032 |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0011"></a>
<a id="g20e01"></a>

### G20E01 · Bulgasari

- Source batch: M031
- Former role class: Boss
- Links: {"houses":["HP06"],"states":["S04","S09"],"theaters":["XT05"]}

