| Common species, variants and command scope | The dark stretch outside the relay niche of the Eastern Command underground duct on the Gwangjin Line, early winter night. |

- The Yagwanggwi stands in the dark duct stretch outside the relay niche.
- Blue light comes from the chest and the backs of the hands.
- The light reflects on the wet duct wall and comes down to the floor.
- A Wall-knocker''s head is turned toward that light.
- The Eastern Command duct watch''s face is inside the blue light.
- A relay-box tag of the Bukhansan Bogukmun Refugee League lies at the edge of the light.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G21-heading-0023"></a>

## Habitat record

Early-winter-night damp has soaked into the relay niche of the Eastern Command underground duct on the Gwangjin Line. The Eastern Command duct watch stands in front of the iron door. Inside the door a person holds the brow to the duct wall.

That person''s mouth and neck are wet, and a gurgle comes from the throat. The brow touches the plate where the heating pipe runs. At each outgoing breath the brow strikes the plate.

The person toward the door strikes once with the brow at each breath. The person in the middle keeps both hands on the rivets and strikes at a short interval. The person toward the junction has both chest and brow flat against the duct wall.

The three people''s chests face the joint plate. The heads are toward the plate where the knocking lingers. The Eastern Command duct watch''s flashlight lights the rivet line of that plate.

Dueoksini is in the junction niche. The head is broader than the shoulders, and the brow presses the upper duct wall. The crown strikes the insulation of the ceiling pipe. The Wall-knockers outside stand along the wall that brow touches.

The Nail-scratcher stands in front of the plate at hand height. The nails are long and the tips are white. The nail tips are in the grooves between the rivets, and the scratched iron shines in the flashlight.

The Yagwanggwi stands in the dark duct outside the niche. Blue light comes from the chest and the backs of the hands. A Wall-knocker''s face is inside that light, and the Amsa–Godeok merchant band''s repair sack lies beside the light.

Waterproof tape and a spare latch from the relay box are in the Eastern Command duct watch''s vest. Spare flashlight cells lie on the box lid. The shift slip of the Eastern Command watch and the Anguk Order watch is stuck to the box lid.

Hangangjin Bridge Council''s lock hangs on the niche latch. A Transmission Relay mark and the Imjin River Gate Theater bypass number are written on the box lid. The Eastern Command duct watch sets the iron-door latch. The watch''s helmet lies on the threshold with a crack in it.
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G22', 'G22 · Flame Lantern', 'bestiary', 22, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

The Flame Lantern carries a blue flame on the wet steel plate of the preservation-vault outer wall, on the siding cars, and at the tips of the spent-battery crystals. The flame is in front of the work lamp and floats low over the steam of the drainage channel. The person, with the flame attached, stands toward the rail and the wall or lies prone on the train roof.

Dokkaebi Fire is the several blue flames floating at the top of the outer wall. Bulgwisin is the person standing on the siding step below, with flame come out past the clothes. Hwama is the form lying prone on the grain-train roof, with the flame of the back laid over the row of cars. The three continue from the preservation-vault outer wall to the Seongha Group siding on the same late-rainy-season night.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | The failed-dehumidifying stretch under the Government of the Republic of Korea and the temporary spent-battery yard of the Changdong Wheel Chamber held water in the same rainy season. Electrolyte crystals stand as metal branches on the steel plate beside the battery boxes, and flame catches at the branch tips. No particular battery or chemical corporation is named. |
| Habitat and movement | The outer wall of the underground preservation vault of the Government of the Republic of Korea at central Seoul Station is where the flame stays. In weeks when yard inspection is late, the flame is at the Seongha Group siding yard on the Gangnam Line. Condensate beads on the roofs of the humid grain trains from the West Sea Granary Theater, and the flame continues beside that condensate. |
| Food and energy | Spent-battery boxes from the Changdong Wheel Chamber sit in the front row of the siding yard. Grain sacks of the West Sea Granary Theater have been moved off the rail from the car where the flame rests. Burned sack cords float on the drainage water. The Seongha Group yard ledger lies open in the breaker hut, and the car numbers are marked in pencil. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | The person who was striking the outer-wall steel plate stands before the same plate. A blue flame is fixed on the back of the hand that was striking. The knees are toward the drainage channel at the foot of the wall, and the flame at the shoulder is in front of the work lamp. |
| Senses | The Flame Lantern''s body is toward the wet steel plate of the outer wall of the underground preservation vault of the Government of the Republic of Korea at central Seoul Station and toward the steam on the roofs of the grain cars on the Seongha Group siding of the Gangnam Line. The head is toward the siding corner. The palms are toward the face of the spent-battery boxes from the Changdong Wheel Chamber where the white crystals stand. |
| Group behavior | Dokkaebi Fire floats at the top of the preservation-vault outer wall. Bulgwisin stands on the siding rail at the foot of the wall, and the face is toward Dokkaebi Fire. Hwama lies prone on the grain-train roof in front of Bulgwisin, and the head is toward the cars whose lids are pale. The people with a point of flame on the back of the hand stand on the steps between the cars. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

Dokkaebi Fire is at the top of the outer wall of the underground preservation vault of the Government of the Republic of Korea at central Seoul Station. Bulgwisin is on the rail from the foot of the wall to the first car of the Seongha Group siding on the Gangnam Line. Hwama is on the roofs from that first car to the rear of the grain train. The people with a point of flame on the back of the hand are on the steps between the cars that Hwama''s flame does not reach.

| Individual | Type | Battlefield unit | Battlefield role | Former role class | Source batch |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| [G22E01 · Dokkaebi Fire](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G22/#g22e01) | Infected person | Single individual | The place where the flames of the upper wall stand at each siding corner | Boss | M034 |
| [G22E08 · Bulgwisin](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G22/#g22e08) | Infected person | Single individual | The place on the step of the first siding car where the body''s flame has come outward | Elite | M035 |
| [G22E15 · Hwama](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G22/#g22e15) | Infected person | Single individual | The place along the grain-train roof where the flame of the back lies | Strategic encounter | M036 |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0011"></a>
<a id="g22e01"></a>

### G22E01 · Dokkaebi Fire

- Source batch: M034
- Former role class: Boss
- Links: {"houses":["HP08"],"states":["S06","S11"],"theaters":["XT02"]}

