| Common species, variants and command scope | It is the stretch where the row of grain-train roofs standing on the Seongha Group siding meets the spent-battery boxes. |

- Hwama lies prone on the roof of the grain train of the West Sea Granary Theater.
- The four feet span the joints of the cars.
- The head is toward the cars whose lids are pale, and the flame of the back lies over the roofs whose lids are curled black.
- The sleeper under the embers fallen from the nose is red.
- The hind feet press on the spent-battery boxes of the Changdong Wheel Chamber.
- Hwama''s head is on the next roof after the car where Bulgwisin stands.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G22-heading-0023"></a>

## Habitat record

The outer wall of the underground preservation vault of the Government of the Republic of Korea at central Seoul Station and the Seongha Group siding of the Gangnam Line meet at the drainage corner. It is a night in the late rainy season. The Seongha Group siding yard duty is in the breaker hut. Water runs on the steel plate of the outer wall. The grain train of the West Sea Granary Theater stands on the siding, and condensate beads on the roofs. Spent-battery boxes from the Changdong Wheel Chamber lean toward the drainage channel, and blue flame spits at the tips of the white crystals.

Dokkaebi Fire floats at the top of the outer wall. The flames are blue and several, and one is low over the steam of the drainage channel. When the yard duty''s work lamp lights the steel plate of a corner, the flame is already at the next corner. A person''s shoulder and hand are inside the largest flame, and the fingertips are bright. The lower side of the flame is toward the wet steel plate and the steam of the car roofs. The place the palms face is the face of the spent-battery boxes where the white crystals stand.

Bulgwisin stands on the step of the first grain car. The flame of the head and shoulders has come out into the night air. The skin is split black, and light comes from the split places. The mouth is open, and the flame inside the mouth is below the chin. Steam stands on the rail under the feet. The sack cords are burned through. Bulgwisin''s face is toward Dokkaebi Fire at the top of the outer wall.

Hwama lies prone on the roof of the grain train. The four feet span the joints of the cars. The head is toward the cars whose lids are pale. The flame of the back lies long over the roofs whose lids are curled black. The sleeper under the embers fallen from the nose is red. Spent-battery boxes are under the hind feet. Bulgwisin stands on the next step of the car that Hwama''s head faces.

On the first night on the same siding a blue flame is a point on the back of a person''s hand. On the next night the flame at the chest shows on the glass of the work lamp. On the night the grain train has come in again, the flame runs along the joints of three cars.

A hand rests on the fist marks of the outer-wall steel plate. A blue flame is fixed on the back of that hand. The same person''s knees are toward the drainage channel at the foot of the wall. The flame at the shoulder is in front of the work lamp.

Dokkaebi Fire is at the top of the outer wall. Bulgwisin stands on the rail at the foot of the wall. Hwama lies prone on the train roof in front of Bulgwisin. The people with a point of flame on the back of the hand stand on the steps between the cars. Spent-battery boxes sit in the front row of the yard. Grain sacks have been moved off the rail from the car where the flame rests. Burned sack cords float on the drainage water.

A Republic of Korea Government duty tag and a Seongha Group duty tag hang side by side in the breaker hut. The Noryangjin Cold-Storage Guild outer-wall key is on the yard duty''s patrol ring. The cell of the Elevator Shaft patrol lamp lies separate on the shelf. The grain train of the West Sea Granary Theater stands on the siding ahead of the Seongha Group yard inspection. The boots of the preservation-vault outer-wall patrol and the boots of the yard duty sit before the same breaker. The siding breaker is down. Fire sand lies the width of the rail in front of the spent-battery boxes. One glove is burned beside the rail. Grain is strewn between the sleepers. The work-lamp glass is split by heat. The yard duty is in the breaker hut with the inspection lamp lit at the siding entrance. The preservation-vault outer-wall patrol stands on the stair inside the corner.
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G23', 'G23 · Udukeoni', 'bestiary', 23, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G23-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G23-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

At midwinter dawn the Udukeoni stand along the cold wall and the coil joints of the defrost corridor. Frost sits on the shoulders and the hair. The chest is still, and the head faces the dark compartment at the end of the corridor. The boots are sunk in the defrost water.

Eoduksini is the place standing at the end of the dark compartment. Teojimi is the place before the joint, with the forearm and the side split. Seorison is the place where frost-covered hands lie across the barrier-door handle and the doorframe. The three are within the line of Udukeoni in the same corridor.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G23-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | The cold-store watch first sees Udukeoni in the defrost corridor at midwinter dawn. A person stands in the corridor. Frost sits on the shoulders and the hair, and both arms hang at the sides. The head is toward the coil housing. The chest is still, and the mouth is closed. The frost at the lips remains as it is. The boots are in the defrost water. / The work lamp is at the corridor entrance. The cold-store watch is on the threshold of the barrier door. Drops from the coil housing fall in front of those boots. |
| Habitat and movement | Udukeoni stand gathered in the defrost corridor. At midwinter dawn, the cold-store watch sees that line from the threshold of the barrier door. The people are along the cold wall, and the gaps between shoulders are much like one another. Frost sits on the shoulders and the hair, and both arms hang at the sides. The chest is still, and the mouth is closed. The head is toward the coil housing. The boots stand in one line of defrost water. The work lamp is at the corridor entrance. / When the season changes and the water on the corridor floor has thawed, the cold-store watch sees the same person from the entrance side. The shoulders are wet, and dried water marks are on the chin and the nape. Drops from the coil housing fall in front of the boots. / Before the compartment at the end of the corridor, the people face the dark. The water on the compartment floor is frozen. The cold-store watch''s flashlight lies on the threshold. |
| Food and energy | A wet blanket and a frost-covered gasket are in the tub. A new rubber gasket and dry gloves hang on the barrier-door latch. One flashlight is on the threshold. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | The same person has dried water marks on the chin and the nape. The shoulders are still. The head is toward the coil, and frost covers the mouth. |
| Senses | The Udukeoni''s head and chest face the defrost coil and the dark compartment at the end of the corridor. The palms rest on the cold doorframe and the pipe joint. |
| Group behavior | Eoduksini stands in the dark compartment at the end of the corridor. Teojimi stands before the coil joint. Seorison has a hand laid over the barrier-door handle. The Udukeoni stand along the cold wall, facing that compartment. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G23-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

Eoduksini is in the dark compartment at the end of the defrost corridor. The Udukeoni stand in one line from the defrost water at the entrance to that compartment. Teojimi is at the joint midway along the line. Seorison is at the barrier door by the entrance.

