- Seorison''s other hand is fixed to the metal of the doorframe.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G23-heading-0023"></a>

## Habitat record

The defrost corridor of the underground cold store is the cold-store watch''s post at midwinter dawn. The defrost water on the corridor floor reaches the boot tops. The cold-store watch is on the dry floor outside the barrier door.

A person stands in the middle of the corridor. Frost sits on the hair and the eyebrows. The eyes are open. Both arms are at the sides. The palms face the cold wall.

The same person has dried water marks on the chin and the nape. The same person''s shoulders are still. The clothing on the chest is dry. Frost remains on the collar.

People stand along the cold wall. The gaps between shoulders are much like one another. Their heads face the dark compartment at the end of the corridor. Their boots are inside the same line of defrost water.

Eoduksini stands in the dark compartment. Eoduksini''s face is in the cold inside the compartment. Eoduksini''s shoulder line meets the light from the entrance. Boot marks on the ice of the compartment floor run up to the front of Eoduksini.

Teojimi stands before the coil joint. Teojimi''s forearm is split lengthwise. The split flesh is pale and wet. The iron plate of the joint is bent out toward the corridor. Frost is lodged on the edge of the plate.

Seorison stands on the inner side of the barrier door. One of Seorison''s hands lies across the handle. The frost on the back of the hand runs past the rubber gasket to the groove under the door. The wet gasket is in the cold-store watch''s tub. The key is in the hand of the boundary watch of the next corridor.
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G24', 'G24 · Weeper', 'bestiary', 24, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

On a midwinter night the wash-room floor is wet with water that has come out of the perfusion piping. The cry runs through the suction pipes and the drain trap and continues into the corridor. At the wet places are the big weeper, the pipe puller, and the Jangsan tiger.

While the big weeper’s cry spreads across the wash-room steel plate, the pipe puller is on its knees at the suction-pipe joint. The Jangsan tiger stands in the dark at the end of the corridor. The child’s cry from the Jangsan tiger’s mouth runs along the corridor and reaches the front of the wash-room door.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | On a midwinter night, the night wash-room duty officer stands in front of the perfusion piping of the night wash room. Water on the floor is up to the ankles, and a cry comes from the suction-pipe joint. The weeper is at that water’s edge, and the face and chest are wet. / The mouth of the person the night wash-room duty officer watched at the same recovery bath is open. From the open mouth the cry spreads into the wash room. Water fallen from the jaw has soaked into the work clothes at the chest. The big weeper stands at the rim of the recovery bath, and both hands are in the water of the recovery bath. |
| Habitat and movement | On a midwinter night, weepers are gathered in the night wash room. The big weeper stands at the rim of the recovery bath. The face and chest are wet, and both hands are in the water of the recovery bath. The cry from the mouth rings the wash-room steel plate. The night wash-room duty officer stands on the floor in front of the perfusion piping, and the water on the floor is up to the ankles. / The pipe puller is on its knees at every suction-pipe joint. The hands grip the pipe mouth, and a wet cassette has gone inside together with the water of the pipe. The head is toward the recovery bath. Beside the big weeper standing at the rim of the recovery bath, the pipe puller’s arm has gone into the suction pipe. A low cry comes from behind the wash-room entry valve, and the water of the recovery bath is touching the night wash-room duty officer’s knees. / At the end of the corridor on the midwinter night, the Jangsan tiger stands on two legs. Pale fur is wet, the back carries a dark tiger pattern, and long hair hangs in front of the face. A child’s cry comes from the Jangsan tiger’s mouth into the corridor, and the night wash-room duty officer’s flashlight is on, on that corridor floor. Empty cassettes are on the service rail of the automatic conveyor, and the bundle of corridor-net treatment records is sunk in the recovery-bath water. |
| Food and energy | The wash-fluid drum is open beside the service rail. Empty cassettes and wet suction pipes are stacked on the automatic conveyor. Water in the recovery bath stands as high as the drain trap. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | The mouth of the person the night wash-room duty officer watched at the same recovery bath, the mouth whose jaw used to strike shut, is open. From the open mouth the cry spreads into the wash room. Water fallen from the jaw has soaked into the work clothes at the chest. |
| Senses | The weeper keeps its chest toward the suction-pipe mouth where the crying comes out and toward the wet floor. When water sounds from the night wash-room duty officer’s boots, the head is toward that water sound. |
| Group behavior | The big weeper stands at the rim of the recovery bath. The pipe puller is on its knees at each suction pipe, and its chest is toward the big weeper. The Jangsan tiger stands on two legs at the end of the corridor, face toward the corridor and back toward the wash room. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

The big weeper is at the rim of the recovery bath, and the cry leaves that place onto the steel plate. The pipe puller is on the suction pipe between the big weeper and the corridor, chest toward the recovery bath. The Jangsan tiger stands farther out on the corridor with its face outward and the wash room behind its back.

| Individual | Type | Battlefield unit | Battlefield role | Former role class | Source batch |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| [G24E01 · Big Weeper](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G24/#g24e01) | Infected person | Single individual | The place of standing at the recovery-bath rim so the cry spreads onto the wash-room steel plate | Boss | M037 |
| [G24E08 · Pipe Puller](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G24/#g24e08) | Infected person | Single individual | The place of keeping a wet cassette and a boot inside the pipe at the suction-pipe joint | Elite | M038 |
| [G24E15 · Jangsan Tiger](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G24/#g24e15) | Infected person | Single individual | The place of standing on two legs at the end of the corridor and sending a child’s cry into the corridor | Strategic encounter | M039 |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0011"></a>
<a id="g24e01"></a>

### G24E01 · Big Weeper

- Source batch: M037
- Former role class: Boss
- Links: {"houses":["HP10"],"states":["S08","S13"],"synthetics":["F08"],"theaters":["XT04"]}

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Infected person |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | The place of standing at the recovery-bath rim so the cry spreads onto the wash-room steel plate |
| Common species, variants and command scope | On a midwinter night it is at the recovery bath of the night wash room, and the pipe puller and the Jangsan tiger are on the piping and in the corridor outside that cry |

- The big weeper stands at the rim of the recovery bath beside the lukewarm perfusion joint.
- The face and chest are wet, and the cry from the mouth rings the wash-room steel plate.
- Both hands are in the recovery-bath water, and steam from the perfusion joint touches the shoulders.
- One record board floats in the water beside the big weeper’s feet.
- While the big weeper’s cry spreads across the steel plate, the pipe puller’s chest is toward the recovery bath.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G24-heading-0015"></a>
<a id="g24e08"></a>

