Interpretation was never turned into an instrument of confession.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0192"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the fracture: the language-pair duty rosters ran short in the interpreter''s booth and at the customs window
- Act 2, the negotiation: Pyo Siwan opened joint inspection against the machine-translation-first rule
- Act 3, the price: interpretation was never turned into an instrument of confession

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0194"></a>

## HC15 · Digital Media City Index House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S09 Yeouido Investment Federation, S16 Jeongdong Federation, S03 Taeuk Group
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Ryu Gaon

Beneath the Sangam transmission tower, the Digital Media City Index House bound severed documents and broadcasts into a single search index.

Each rumor carried a verification table and a counter-argument timestamp, so that verdicts themselves could not be traded.

Ryu Gaon published the Suseo contract ledgers side by side with the advertisement-slot bidding records.

The Magok researchers appended to the earlier verdicts whenever the evidence changed, and never erased them.

Even when buyers paid for ranking, they could not touch the evidence lines under the search results.

When the protection-treaty violation record vanished, the index keeper and the auction observer each opened a different vault.

Instead of exposing the manipulation, the Digital Media City Index House gave up its largest advertisement slot and its southern passage rights.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0203"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the omission: the Suseo protection-treaty violation record disappeared from the Sangam tower index
- Act 2, the bid: Ryu Gaon staked the same rebuttal time for the Magok verifier and the advertisement-slot buyer
- Act 3, the trace: after the award ledger was published, the Digital Media City Index House lost its most expensive advertisement slot

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0205"></a>

## HC16 · Yongsan Exchange House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S09 Yeouido Investment Federation, S07 The Junction, S12 Sinnae Transport
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Antoine Lefebvre

In the Yongsan rail warehouse, the switchboard of the Yongsan Exchange House carried words between Sangam and Sinnae.

The trackside base station borrowed freight-truck batteries to keep a short relay stretch alive.

Users of the leased lines were set not by the track houses but by call order.

When a downpour snapped the rooftop relay, the Sinnae patient-transport signal was the first to move onto the detour line.

The freight merchants demanded a dedicated line to cover their losses, and the subscribers'' delegate blocked it.

As the price of the revived route, the Yongsan Exchange House handed over the operating rights to one bay of the Yongsan exchange room.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0213"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the severance: the warehouse switchboard went dark, and the Sinnae medical-train call could not reach Sangam
- Act 2, the bypass: The freight dispatch circuits were reduced, and a temporary relay was connected on the railway roof.
- Act 3, the cession: the price of saving the medical calls was one bay of the exchange, ceded to the Yongsan track house

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0215"></a>

## HC17 · Guro Digital Complex Battery House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S02 The Gauge, S04 Myeongbu Church, S11 Seongha Group
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Byeon Jua

Along the Guro–Geumcheon production axis, the Guro Digital Complex Battery House sorted loose battery cells into stacks by lifespan and temperature.

The Ttukseom workshop took sealed electrolyte drums and built power bundles for pumps and small machines.

The Changdong rolling-stock depot demanded its braking stock first, and accepted no material without a test certificate.

When one leaking drum was found, every bundle on the same freight cart went into quarantine.

The production repair crews pressed for the shortage to be released, and the northern technicians blocked the warehouse door to hold the braking share.

After the materials certifier uncovered forged markings, the supply order changed to an open draw among three states.

To keep its trust, the Guro Digital Complex Battery House discarded even usable cells and cut Changdong''s reserve runs.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0224"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the leak: an electrolyte drum in the Guro–Geumcheon stockpile leaked, and even the Ttukseom certificates came under doubt
- Act 2, the allocation: The Changdong braking-battery share was sealed while the retesting order was disputed with the production-alliance repair crews.
- Act 3, the scrapping: the contaminated bundles were discarded whole, and one reserve run of the northern trains was given up

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0226"></a>

## HC18 · Yongsan Ship House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S07 The Junction, S08 Central Intelligence Bureau, S15 Myeongdong Archdiocese
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Pieter Jansen

Under the rusted cranes of the Yongsan north bank, the Yongsan Ship House assigned the barge berths.

A cold box loaded at Noryangjin reached the Garak wholesale auction floor only with its seal tag intact.

The old air-cargo standard survived as a ledger rule separating weight from liability for damage.

The shipowners demanded faster routes, and the landing inspectors confirmed the priority of public freight.

When a grounded ship blocked the channel, three states each pressed their wharf rights.

The Yongsan Ship House gave up its exclusive berth and, in exchange, published every stevedoring fee and sailing order.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0234"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the locked wharf: a ship grounded under the Han River bridges jammed the Yongsan riverside logistics and the barge routes at once
- Act 2, the price of the three landings: Wharf negotiations tied the Noryangjin cold freight to access at the Garak auction.
- Act 3, the route of the empty boxes: the exclusive wharf was given up, and one berth ledger covered every sealed consignment

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0236"></a>

## HC19 · Dongdaeipgu Trading House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S06 Republic of Korea Government, S15 Myeongdong Archdiocese, S16 Jeongdong Federation
- Exclusive states: None

Along the protocol road at Seoul Station stood the neutral guest lodges kept by the Dongdaeipgu Trading House.

An envoy who had surrendered weapons was still not detained over lodging debts.

Banquet goods were bought at open auction in the Garak wholesale market and tagged item by item.

The old bonded warehouse filled less with splendid goods than with handicrafts owed as treaty gifts.

On short rations the banquet tables thinned first, and the ordinary guests'' porridge stayed as it was.

When a hidden guarantor came to light, the guest-observer cancelled the trade regardless of protocol rank.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0244"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the empty banquet seats: ahead of the Seoul Station protocol talks, the banquet-goods delivery tags vanished from the Garak auction
- Act 2, the ledger of entertainment: The Suseo contract audit exposed the hidden guarantor behind room assignments and banquet credit.
- Act 3, the gift left outside the gate: the privileged guests'' bonded warehouse was opened, and famine rations were parted from diplomatic return gifts

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0246"></a>

## HC20 · Digital Media City Performance House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S06 Republic of Korea Government, S15 Myeongdong Archdiocese, S09 Yeouido Investment Federation
- Exclusive states: None

Every evening the Sangam transmission tower lit, the Digital Media City Performance House sealed the performance order.

A performer who took the Seoul Station protocol stage had name and return passage guaranteed under the Records Bureau''s accreditation.

At the Garak assembly ground, every three paid tickets left one refugee seat open.

When the channel guild pushed popularity rankings alone, the audience observer suspended the programming meeting.

The forged-ticket uproar shook not only the ticket revenue but the tower''s verification trust as well.

The Digital Media City Performance House divided the final broadcast hours among the states'' testimonies and published the release of its exclusive rights.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0254"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the broken refrain: one Seoul Station protocol performance was struck from the tower''s prime-time schedule
- Act 2, the crowd without tickets: As forged tickets spread through the Garak assembly ground, the performance-rights ledger was compared with broadcast records.
- Act 3, the last broadcast: the exclusive performance rights were loosed for a moment, and every state''s testimony went out in the same broadcast hours

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0256"></a>

## HC21 · Digital Media City Payments House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S09 Yeouido Investment Federation, S16 Jeongdong Federation, S12 Sinnae Transport
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Yong So

From the basement relay room of an old Sangam office block, the Digital Media City Payments House kept the transfer-payment lines.

When the Suseo charter city demanded notarized ledgers, only audit read-access was opened, and the signing key was never handed over.

The call window of Sinnae Transport was fenced with queue rules so that no faction''s troops could jump the line.

Even with the lines dead, the last settlement block stayed on paper.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0262"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, the severance: ledger sync with Suseo broke, and the transfer calls piled up
- Act 2, Relay: Negotiations opened to divide the circuits for Sangam transmission verification and Sinnae transfer neutrality.
- Act 3, the circuit: the message relay was cut back, but the payment ledger survived whole

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0264"></a>

## HC22 · Magok Test-Line House

- Class: CORPORATION
- Status: ACTIVE
- Linked states: S03 Taeuk Group, S09 Yeouido Investment Federation, S11 Seongha Group
- Exclusive states: None
- Steward: Choi Eunjae

Beside the autonomous test line at the edge of the Magok research grounds, the Magok Test-Line House kept the energy-storage depot.

If the old insect-, dinosaur-, and deep-form test units move again beneath the line, only half of the drawing key is brought out and kept under the Magok council''s watch.

When the Changdong depot''s charging circuits turned unstable, the certification was closed for a while and the circuits were settled first.

Even with the depot empty, the certification seal was never forged.

<a id="Operating-Houses-heading-0270"></a>

### Three acts

- Act 1, Alarm: Residual signals from the lost technology line beneath the Magok test line rose again
- Act 2, the division: The drawing key was split between the Magok council and the Sangam works.
- Act 3, the seal: the test line went back under lock, and only the charging standard remained
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('Oral-Stories', 'The Stories', 'culture', 3, '
A. The waterworks operations log

At about 21:47 on October 14, 2030, remote control failed at the Yeongdeungpo waterworks. Duty officer Han Jeonghun operated the valves manually and entered the failure in the first line of a paper operations log.


## The Blackout of October 14, 2030

A. Crisis room report

At about 21:47 on October 14, 2030, district indicators went dark in sequence at the Blue House crisis center. Night officer Yun Taesik tried to report to the National Security Office and Joint Chiefs, but the lines did not connect.

B. Emergency order

On October 15, 2030, the president wrote and signed an emergency order under Article 76 of the constitution. The prime minister countersigned it. Designated facility emergency officers received on-site authority during the communications outage.


## The 2026 Water and Parts Exchange

A. November 6 exchange

On November 6, 2026, two Yeouido vault representatives visited the Yeongdeungpo waterworks. Han Jeonghun agreed to open the valve toward Yeouido from 06:00 to 12:00 daily in exchange for two emergency generator parts.

B. Two ledgers

Han Jeonghun entered the exchange in the operations log. The Yeouido vault also entered the parts and water exchange in its inventory under the same date.


## The 2053 Yeongdeungpo Water Agreement

A. March 14 signatures

On March 14, 2053, waterworks head Han Seokjin and six water-receiving family representatives met seven Yeouido family representatives. Fourteen representatives signed an agreement transferring management of eleven water facilities near Yeouido and Yeongdeungpo Station to the Yeouido families.

B. Move to Yangpyeong Station

From March 20, 2053, the Yeongdeungpo waterworks staff moved their base to Yangpyeong Station underground. Forty-five volumes of the waterworks operations log, including Han Jeonghun’s forty-one volumes, moved to the underground stacks there. The waterworks continued operating.


## Registers and Contracts

A. Waterway contract

In June 2097, Sumunguk contracted with waterway workers in Yangpyeong and Chuncheon. They were entered in the Yangpyeong Station ration register in return for managing the waterways.

B. Reconstruction worker register

In winter 2120, Dongbangsa demanded registration of reconstruction workers from Gyugyeokmaeng in exchange for pump parts. Gang Minseo placed workers who refused in the civic register.

C. Refugee register

In 2123, a refugee procession from Bukhansan Bogukmun descended toward Anguk.

D. Three contracts

In 2123, Sumunguk, Gyugyeokmaeng, and Hwanjeokguk sent separate water, parts, and transit contracts to the minor states in the same week. Jeong Yura copied their end conditions into one document.

E. State ledger

In November 2125, the records office compiled a power ranking of sixteen states.


## Sources

- [Seoul Subway States Timeline 2026–2126](/wiki/Century-Annals/)
- [Scenario Timeline](/wiki/Scenario-Timeline/)
- [The Faith-and-Culture Schism](/wiki/Faith-Culture-Schism/)
- [Food Culture](/wiki/Food-Culture/)
- [The Sixteen States of Seoul](/wiki/Sixteen-States/)
- [The Great Blackout](/wiki/World-Unbinding/)
- [The Structures Compendium](/wiki/Structures/)
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, category_id, sort, body_md) VALUES ('People-and-Machines', 'People and Machines', 'people-and-machines', 0, '
**A. How people and machines are placed**

In the Seoul of 2126, at the opening, the bodies that founded states remained human. They slept in the concourses of Yeongdeungpo, Seoul Station, and Amsa, stood sluice watch, and lined up at the ration windows. In the same graph, stopped arms mixed with machines that still walked, and raptors, feral dogs, and rat swarms clung to the rations, the heat, and the wetlands. This was not a list that tried to revive in numbers the density of the years when the call network lived; it was a compendium that recorded what the Great Blackout cut off and what remained inside the stations.

On October 15, 2030, the president signed an emergency order authorizing designated facility officers to act on site during the communications outage. Yeongdeungpo waterworks staff manually operated valves that day.


## People

**A. Watch duty and livelihood**

On October 14, 2030, Yeongdeungpo waterworks officer Han Jeonghun started a paper operations log after remote control failed. In 2053, forty-five volumes of the waterworks center''s operations logs, including forty-one of Han''s, were moved to the underground stacks of Yangpyeong Station.

In 2106, the Republic of Korea required a Government Seoul Complex stamp on Jongno and Junggu passes. Commercial contracts needed that stamp for registration.

In winter 2120, Dongbangsa demanded registration of reconstruction workers from Gyugyeokmaeng. Gang Minseo entered those who refused in its civic register.

When the water was cut, labor folded first. Even when food ran short, the next day''s hands slowed, and without medicine the act of treatment itself did not open. The way the illnesses of people and of the tanks overlapped at one window was covered by [Ailments and Symptoms](/wiki/Ailments/).


## The Remnants of Logistics Humanoids

**A. The 2026 field trials**

The robot density of Korean manufacturing in 2026 was recorded as 1,012 units per 10,000 workers, and the model field humanoid was Boston Dynamics'' Atlas. Material transport with minimal supervision and trials on Hyundai Motor sites were that year''s starting point ([Atlas](https://www.bostondynamics.com/atlas), accessed 2026-09-17; [IFR 2024-11-20](https://ifr.org/ifr-press-releases/news/global-robot-density-in-factories-doubled-in-seven-years), accessed 2026-09-17). After the calls were cut, there was no foundry to lay the same line anew.

The bodies that remained at the opening fell into two kinds: remnants standing with frozen joints at their charging terminals, and remnants repeating only their last transport order. The maintenance sheds of the Guro complex blocks and the Cheonwang depot side, and the sealed cells of the Magok test section, were often named as their places. Mechanics swapped hoses, terminals, and lenses to make pumps and watch stoves, but they could not repair the neural-network weights as a whole. The lock that kept knowing, holding, repairing, and manufacturing out of a single sentence was in [Lost Technology](/wiki/Lost-Technology-Lineage/).

After the Great Blackout cut machines off from the upper control network, they repeated their last assigned search and guard tasks.

At the opening, I Yeon is a biological synthetic humanoid in Jo Jaepyo''s company. The H01–H16 register instead records mechanical humanoids under house custody. Neither the kind of body alone grants nor denies personhood or citizenship. Each individual is assessed for expressed will, continuity of memory, and capacity to consent. A custody record can document maintenance and responsibility, but its transfer clause cannot govern someone recognized as a person. I Yeon records her own courier judgment under her name and refuses an order that would sacrifice civilians. No such individual determination is recorded for the H01–H16 actors.


## Repeating Machines

**A. Surviving disaster-response machines**

There were bodies that overlapped with the logistics humanoids but did not stand in the same line. They were machines that pre-collapse disaster agencies had meant to use for search, reinforcement, and pipe inspection, and when the upper control network fell away, they continued the search, guard, and transport routines they had last received, subject to their stored charge and access to charging terminals. Small swarms that glowed like lanterns, heavy machines that pushed rubble with hydraulics, and flat underwater shells were those three lines. The line names and seal coordinates were a creative layer, and this page did not prove any list of real 2026 deployments.

The triggers for restart were voltage, water level, and authorization signals. Stations with attached depots such as Sinjeong, Gunja, and Godeok, water treatment with attached sluices such as Yeongdeungpo, Ttukseom, and Amsa, and the galleries of the deep tunnels provided that stage. When a scout thrust a protocol card forward, only that line, that trigger point, and that command bundle could be paused for a while; there was no universal control. The detailed modules and the salvage economy were recorded by [Lost Technology](/wiki/Lost-Technology-Lineage/), and this compendium fixed only which mission''s echo the machines still walking beside people were.

Capacitor modules only used the charge already stored and could not replace generators; cells aged, and without charging terminals the repetition broke off too. A workshop repairing hydraulics did not make it look as if the fabs had returned.


## Raptors, Feral Dogs, and Rat Swarms

**A. Rations and wild animals**

The more stable human rations became, the more animal density followed those windows. At dusk, flocks of crows settled on the transmission towers of Sangam and Nanji, the cables of the Han bridges, and the Yongsan catenary, while the waste heat of factory roofs and the sparks of overhead lines drew insects. People called them the Large-billed Crow, but the flock did not read the content of the radio waves; it learned only the order of sparks, work noise, and food. In the spring breeding season, the bridges, school passages, and the tops of evacuation stairs became circles of diving attacks. The index was the Large-billed Crow in the [Bestiary of Ecology and Variants](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/), and the field page was [G02](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G02/).

Feral dogs formed families along the walls of the Magok laboratories, in closed security passages, and on weedy lots, and at night they went down as far as the Noryangjin fish docks. Their rusted collar rings made a clinking of iron, so they were named the Feral Dog. They were closer to the result of the habits of 2026, when private shelters closed their doors and construction-site guard dogs lost their people in the evacuation columns, clinging for a century to dock leftovers and the sound of ration-cart wheels. The leader was not fixed. The coexisting kind that walked beside the ration carts was a learning of the same pack. [G03](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G03/).

Rats made states at the transfers. Where crumbs and the heat of insulated pipes overlapped at the junctions where the Gangdong-Amsa ration passages met the Eunpyeong-Seongbuk evacuation stairs, two or three core nests formed under the cable trays. The colonies were not locked as hosts of any special plague. They were only a density of food, warmth, and shelter. When their droppings damaged wire insulation, the guidance displays went dark, and in the dark passages people thought of contagion first. [G05](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G05/).

On the wetlands of the Han, Nanji, and Amsa and the drainage ponds of the Changdong depot, waterfowl and waders settled first, and when the food rose, raptors followed onto the wires. When the sluices were lowered unilaterally, the flocks shot up over the depot tracks and blocked the train movements. The name binding migratory birds and predatory birds into one colony was creative, but the stopovers of the Han and the depot ponds were places that existed in 2026 as well. [G06](/wiki/Hostile-Group-G06/).

Sweeping up the swarms with firearms was left as a last resort. Sealing, ration detours, and the collection of leftovers were closer to what guarded the human windows. Why the stations, tunnels, and depots were the skeleton of those windows was connected by [The Structures Compendium](/wiki/Structures/).

| Layer | 2026 starting point | What remained at the 2126 opening |
|---|---|---|
| People | Subway living spheres, military registers, trade sites | The sixteen states of station strongholds, paper registers, the seven trades |
| Logistics humanoids | Atlas-class field trials, factory density at the front of the world | Stopped remnants and repeated transport, dismantled modules |
| Disaster machines | Search, guard, and transport routines tied to the call network | Search and guard routines in sealed galleries stop when batteries fail or charging is lost. [Lost Technology](/wiki/Lost-Technology-Lineage/) |
| Raptors, feral dogs, rats | Han River birds, abandoned dogs, station rats | Colonies on the towers, the docks, and the transfer trays |


## Sources

- [Characters, Factions, and Trades](/wiki/Characters-Factions-and-Professions/)
- [Scenario Timeline](/wiki/Scenario-Timeline/)
- [The Sixteen States of Seoul](/wiki/Sixteen-States/)
- [The Arms and Technology of This Era](/wiki/Era-Arms-and-Tech-Level/)
- [The Great Blackout](/wiki/World-Unbinding/)
- [River, Gu, and Dong Building Reuse](/wiki/Building-Reuse-Geography/)
');
